<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 19.07 pct in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 19.07 pct in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	19.07	    + 36	    18.95     19.25</p>
<p>90-Day	20.34	    + 71	    20.22     20.40</p>
<p>182-Day     21.30	    + 53	    20.95     21.41</p>
<p>343-Day     21.02				20.94     21.09</p>
<p>Last week the 350-day paper was assigned at 20.84 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   1.63 bln pesos    2.04</p>
<p>90-Day	1.2 million pesos   3.65 bln pesos    3.04</p>
<p>182-Day     1.2 million pesos   2.66 bln pesos    2.22</p>
<p>343-Day     1.0 million pesos   2.99 bln pesos    2.99</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 2.60 on demand of 10.93 billion pesos compared to 2.91 the week before on demand of 10.49 billion pesos the week before. Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   18 basis points</p>
<p>    90-Day			    6 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  11 basis points</p>
<p>    343-Day			   7 basis points</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9507))</p>
</text>
